WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.267
-Welcome, back,
everybody,

00:00:02.267 --> 00:00:03.367
We're talking with
Sigourney Weaver

00:00:03.367 --> 00:00:07.400
who stars in the new movie
"Call Jane,"

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:09.801
which opens this Friday.

00:00:09.801 --> 00:00:11.667
You're fantastic in this movie.

00:00:11.667 --> 00:00:15.534
The movie is fantastic
and very important,

00:00:15.534 --> 00:00:18.667
oddly for these times,
now.

00:00:18.667 --> 00:00:21.000
But can you explain
who you play,

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.601
and what the movie is about?

00:00:22.601 --> 00:00:27.501
-So "Call Jane" was the name of
a clandestine organization

00:00:27.501 --> 00:00:30.000
put together by women
to help women

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.634
obtain safe illegal abortions.

00:00:33.634 --> 00:00:36.834
And it's this group of women who
just come together to, you know,

00:00:36.834 --> 00:00:40.968
with respect,
and real love and care,

00:00:40.968 --> 00:00:45.267
to take all these different
women, with different reasons,

00:00:45.267 --> 00:00:46.634
but good reasons,

00:00:46.634 --> 00:00:50.200
who had to take advantage
of that procedure.

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:52.033
And we follow the great
Elizabeth Banks...

00:00:52.033 --> 00:00:53.067
-She's fantastic.

00:00:53.067 --> 00:00:54.634
...who plays a
housewife named Joy.

00:00:54.634 --> 00:00:56.033
You follow her story.

00:00:56.033 --> 00:01:00.968
And she has a kind of
political awakening.

00:01:00.968 --> 00:01:03.167
And I'm hoping that the movie,
because it sort of --

00:01:03.167 --> 00:01:04.868
first of all, it's very
entertaining.

00:01:04.868 --> 00:01:08.200
It's not like taking, like, a
bottle of medicine or anything.

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:10.701
-No, no, no.
-You know, it's got jokes.

00:01:10.701 --> 00:01:12.400
-Yes.
-Um, and...

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:13.734
and my character
is quite funny.

00:01:13.734 --> 00:01:16.534
But, you know, we're hoping
that it will sort of

00:01:16.534 --> 00:01:18.033
de politicize this,

00:01:18.033 --> 00:01:20.667
remind people that the person
who's really at risk

00:01:20.667 --> 00:01:22.167
is the woman,

00:01:22.167 --> 00:01:23.701
and that she needs
all the support

00:01:23.701 --> 00:01:25.300
and compassion
we can give her.

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:26.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:26.968 --> 00:01:28.067
-Absolutely.
-Yeah.

00:01:28.067 --> 00:01:29.100
-It's...

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:31.467
[ Cheers and applause
continues ]

00:01:31.467 --> 00:01:38.000
It's so -- when you see it,
you go, "Oh, my gosh."

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:42.901
The story is -- amazing, and
some intense moments, as well.

00:01:42.901 --> 00:01:45.734
But then I was asking you,
when did you film this?

00:01:45.734 --> 00:01:50.133
-Yeah, we filmed it
in the spring of '21.

00:01:50.133 --> 00:01:55.000
So we -- we were not -- I was
not expecting Roe Versus Wade,

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:58.901
this thing had transformed
women's lives,

00:01:58.901 --> 00:02:02.934
given them a chance
to control when they have

00:02:02.934 --> 00:02:05.467
their families, and how many
children they have,

00:02:05.467 --> 00:02:08.667
and, you know,

00:02:08.667 --> 00:02:12.167
we didn't imagine that it could
be overturned in such a way.

00:02:12.167 --> 00:02:13.701
-Yeah.
-And now we're --

00:02:13.701 --> 00:02:16.367
this is unfortunately,
especially relevant.

00:02:16.367 --> 00:02:19.801
And we're hoping that
in the midterms, you know,

00:02:19.801 --> 00:02:21.834
that it will be very much
on people's minds,

00:02:21.834 --> 00:02:25.901
and that this movie can help
encourage people to vote,

00:02:25.901 --> 00:02:28.200
vote back our rights.

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:29.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:29.734 --> 00:02:31.033
-That's right.

00:02:31.033 --> 00:02:32.167
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:02:32.167 --> 00:02:34.334
Here's Sigourney weaver
in "Call Jane."

00:02:34.334 --> 00:02:35.901
Take a look at this.
-Okay.

00:02:35.901 --> 00:02:37.334
-Well done, Jackie O.

00:02:38.767 --> 00:02:41.200
I'm sorry that wasn't the
morning you expected.

00:02:43.968 --> 00:02:45.634
-You read my mind, Doll.

00:02:45.634 --> 00:02:47.033
-[ Chuckles ]

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:48.934
-Mm-mm-mm.

00:02:48.934 --> 00:02:49.968
-I'm trying to quit.

00:02:51.501 --> 00:02:53.067
-Why?

00:02:53.067 --> 00:02:56.100
-Maybe I want to sing opera
in my next life.

00:02:58.033 --> 00:03:02.033
-We have organizing meetings
on Thursdays.

00:03:03.234 --> 00:03:05.400
That's the address.

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:07.400
[ Soft jazz music plays ]

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:11.601
♪♪

00:03:11.601 --> 00:03:13.767
-I don't agree with
what you're doing.

00:03:13.767 --> 00:03:15.234
-Sigourney weaver,
everybody.

00:03:15.234 --> 00:03:16.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:20.300
"Call Jane" opens in
theaters this Friday.

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:22.100
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:23.467
We love it every time
you're here.

00:03:23.467 --> 00:03:24.467
Sigourney weaver!

00:03:24.467 --> 00:03:25.467
More "Tonight Show"
after the break.

00:03:25.467 --> 00:03:26.467
Stick around.

